\tag{fdip}
\title{Cochains, Stokes and Hodge theory}
\date{2026-11-02}

\p{What replaces a derivative when the only space is a grid? The
[zero-mode count](fdip-000T) for the centered Dirac operator gives
#{\dim_{\mathbb C}\ker D=2^{d+e}}, where #{e} is the number of even
periods among #{N_1,\ldots,N_d}. For #{d=2} that dimension is
#{2^{2+e}}, so it changes when a side length changes parity.}

\p{The square cell complex on the same vertices does not. For every
pair of positive integers, the coboundary composed with itself is
zero and the real cohomology has dimensions #{(1,2,1)}. The
following section takes up the adjoint of this coboundary.}

\transclude{fdip-008Z}
